From 07dc3b9e3256a7ff389cd1981de00e84a5d4e895 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:53:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 568/572] fix(stm32mp2): update support for PSCI_OS_INIT_MODE

Since commit 9bf7047a4f8f5601 ("feat(psci): add hierarchical power
state consistency check") the power state must be consistent for
PSCI OSI support but it is not the case for STM32MP2 LP-Stop1 modes
when the other core is just in standby with PWRSTATE_RUN.

This patch updates the values of psci-suspend-param and PWRSTATE
to allow this hierarchical consistency check without error.

STM32MP2 use 5 levels in the topology, to handle LPLV-STOP specific
treatment in SPD OP-TEE with cpu_suspend_entry parameter
"max_off_pwrlvl, and with possible state value between at each
power level: 0(RUN), 1(RET), 2(LP) and 3(OFF):

    0: (2) CPU1 core#0 / CPU1 core#1
    1: (1) CLUSTER / D1 Domain
    2: (1) LPLV D1
    3: (1) D2
    4: (1) LPLV D2 : SoC

The PSCI PM idle state uses the recommended encoding for State-ID
in PSCI 1.0 Specification, with extended State-ID formats.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git f3bb4f50d75c2b5b183796dea20f219d5e0e1ba5 fix(stm32mp2): update support for PSCI_OS_INIT_MODE]
